# React / Next.js Rules

## Project Structure (src/)

```zsh
src/
├── app/
│   ├── (auth)/           # login, register
│   ├── (app)/            # protected: dashboard, settings
│   ├── api/              # route handlers
│   └── layout.tsx
├── components/
│   ├── ui/               # base UI
│   ├── forms/            # form components
│   └── features/         # feature components
└── lib/
    ├── auth/
    ├── db/
    └── validations/
```

## App Router

- Pages: `src/app/[route]/page.tsx`
- Layouts: `src/app/layout.tsx`
- API: `src/app/api/[route]/route.ts`

## Server vs Client Components

Default: Server Components. Add `'use client'` only when needed for:

- Event handlers (onClick, onChange)
- React hooks (useState, useEffect)
- Browser APIs (localStorage, window)
- Effector stores or other client state

## Data & State

| Type        | Use                          |
|-------------|------------------------------|
| Server data | Server Components, Suspense  |
| Client data | TanStack Query               |
| Global      | Effector                     |
| URL         | searchParams                 |
| Local UI    | useState / useReducer        |

## Server Actions

- For mutations (create, update, delete)
- Validate input with Zod
- Return unified Result type
- Handle errors gracefully

## proxy.ts (not middleware.ts)

Next.js deprecated `middleware.ts`. Use `proxy.ts` instead:

- File: `src/proxy.ts`
- Export: `proxy(request)`, not `middleware`
- Use for: auth redirects, rate limiting, security headers

## Index Files

- Every reusable folder has `index.ts` as public API
- External imports: `import { X } from '@/components/ui'` (not `from './button'`)
- Exception: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `route.ts` — no index needed
